{
  "manifestId": "portfolio-scope-parity",
  "version": "2.1.0",
  "modelVersion": "1.2.5",
  "purpose": "Neutral, serializable fixtures for the cross-tier Portfolio scope parity contract (PST-PARITY-001..005). Revision 2.1.0 RECONCILES THE QUANTITY OWNER: one residual vocabulary, one precedence, one presence rule, one invalid-value rule, one gross fallback and one side/sign rule across both tiers, plus the close-marker set the frontend Journal actually writes. Every `expected` block is GENERATED by the backend owner portfolioScopeCanonicalOutcome(), so no tier can hold a second opinion about what the other produces. A mismatch of manifest version, manifest sha256 or scope-semantics version makes the run UNAVAILABLE with PORTFOLIO_SCOPE_PARITY_DIVERGENCE.",
  "generatedBy": "scripts/generate-portfolio-scope-parity-manifest.mjs — expected blocks come from lib/portfolio-journal-scope.js portfolioScopeCanonicalOutcome()",
  "shaScope": "sha256 over the canonical JSON of the `fixtures` array only, so prose edits above do not churn the hash",
  "sha256": "5dff46fb958c728ae48326a510fc79e6e5a94a8a85608b91538400125ec5d0cb",
  "producerAudit": {
    "finding": "NOT ONE of the eighteen residual alias names carried by the two tiers has a producer. Each occurs exactly once in its own declaring array literal. The frontend Journal closes a leg by writing status, exitPrice, closePrice and closeDate; it has no partial-close UI and never writes a residual quantity. `leg.qty` is the only quantity any producer writes; `quantity` is echoed by the enriched endpoint.",
    "consequence": "The canonical vocabulary is a DECLARATION, not a discovery, and is recorded as one. It is the UNION of what the two tiers already claimed to honour — narrowing it would mean one tier silently ignoring a field the other reads — and the precedence is pinned by fixtures wherever two aliases disagree, so the choice cannot drift once a producer finally appears.",
    "realProducers": {
      "quantity": [
        "qty",
        "quantity",
        "contracts"
      ],
      "residual": [],
      "closeMarkers": [
        "exitPrice",
        "closePrice",
        "closeDate",
        "exitSnapshot"
      ]
    }
  },
  "consumerContract": {
    "backend": "tests/portfolio-scope-parity.test.js regenerates every expected block from the owners and asserts the committed manifest matches",
    "frontend": "the companion PR in apex-trading loads this manifest and produces identical outcomes from its own scope owners; it holds no expected table of its own",
    "onDivergence": "the stress run is UNAVAILABLE with reason PORTFOLIO_SCOPE_PARITY_DIVERGENCE"
  },
  "expectedFields": [
    "tradeOpen",
    "legOpen",
    "quantity",
    "signedQuantity",
    "quantityStatus",
    "quantitySource",
    "quantityReason",
    "positionSide",
    "isZeroResidual",
    "carriesCurrentRisk",
    "terminalReason"
  ],
